# 2024.11.18
# The 3K alfalfa DArTag panel was developed for 54-bp amplicons;
# DArT now generates 81-bp amplicons, so my initial plan is to extend all microhaplotypes to 81 bp based on the reference genome
# Andrew Farmer used these extended 81 bp microhaplotypes to check genome assemblies of 10 alfalfa lines,
# where he found the extended bases interfered with the QC.
# I will need to remove those extended bases of all RefMatch and AltMatch alleles.

# Alfalfa v003-4 has RefMatch and AltMatch alleles extended from 54 bp to 81 bp
# Alfalfa v017 has RefMatch and AltMatch alleles extended from 54-81 bp (sequenced to 81 bp at DArT) to 81 bp
# The plan is to
# 1. Check all the versions of database to make sure they were processed using 10 samples as missing data threshold for keeping microhaplotypes
# 2. Retain 54 bp of RefMatch and AltMatch alleles from v004 because those data were generated based on 54 bp amplicons
# 3. Get the non-extended microhaplotypes from v016, where data were generated based on 81 bp amplicons
# 4. Generate an updated database with all RefMatch and AltMatch with their original amplicon lengths (54-81 bp)

# /Users/dz359/PycharmProjects/BI/alfalfa_dartag_00_microhaplotype_db/data/alfalfa_allele_db_v004.fa
# Number of RefMatch and AltMatch alleles that should be reverted back to 54 bp sequence: 5002
{'>chr1.1_000194324|AltMatch_0001': 54, '>chr1.1_000309952|AltMatch_0001': 54, '>chr1.1_000532584|RefMatch_0001': 54, '>chr1.1_000532584|RefMatch_0002': 54, '>chr1.1_000532584|RefMatch_0003': 54}
# /Users/dz359/PycharmProjects/BI/alfalfa_dartag_00_microhaplotype_db/data/alfalfa_allele_db_v016.fa
# Number of RefMatch and AltMatch alleles that should be reverted back to actual amplicon sequences: 12467
